From 174ead5cace018c9d0a10ee45067ca5536df743d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:16:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ggml: add GGML_TYPE_SX8 (57), the S-X8 v4.3 CPU decoder,
 retagged from the author's 41, plus its retag/cross-check tooling

The S-X8 weight format (dmin/dmax f16 + 4 x 2-bit range strategy + 6-bit levels, 30 B / 32, 7.50 bpw) lands as type id 57 under the fork's type-id arbitration (research/local-inference/2026-08-15-ggml-type-id-arbitration.md): the author ships it at 41, which this tree already spends, so the port retags to the next free id above ESCHA3/56. CPU decoder only - dequant, vec_dot, and the GET_ROWS / CPY / SET_ROWS arms - plus gguf-py constants and test-backend-ops coverage.

Opt-in by TYPE NAME and nothing else: no env, no build flag, no default moved. GGML_TYPE_SX8 is reachable only when a tensor or a -ctk/-ctv argument names it, so every launch that does not is byte-identical to the pre-commit engine.

tools/gguf-retag-sx8: retag_sx8.py rewrites an author-tagged file's type ids to 57 on a COPY, and test_sx8_codec.py cross-checks our decoder against the author's reference; the codec cross-check loads the ggml DLLs with the legacy Windows search (winmode=0), which is what makes it run at all on this box.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-212 R18 WI-1692 (Fable 5.1 MEDIUM, kernel-maker), POOL MODE code half
Taken-from: MarlaLabs llama-cpp-sx8.patch (github.com/MarlaLabs, Apache-2.0), cloned at cache/r16-sx8
Measured-effect: DOCUMENTED-TAKE. The harmless cell (the port present but unreachable) read DFlash2 decode +0.43% CI95 [-0.47%, +1.33%] and plain decode -5.33% [-12.26%, +1.60%]; the same pair moved plain PREFILL -8.28% [-11.00%, -5.56%], the wave's largest inert move, which is the build floor and not this port. TBO ladder x0.991 to x1.033. The S-X8 file cell never ran: no S-X8 file exists and the decoder is CPU-only.
Owed: the Vulkan kernel (WI-1717, lane-224) builds ON this enum - it must not re-add id 57.
Cherry-picked-from: 3c6022780237b5485596379aeff653da4e640f9b and 6917b82bc862b0426744fc53ce077f0728885022 (lane-212/wi1692-sx8-port-2026-09-06, b10819 base)
WI: WI-1692
Lane: lane-225
